From 5890bec5f44f493f105fea7c3bd6bb28fdd2f98a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:28:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the context ring's usage card and its report
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.34 (asks 57, 58). A click on the context ring opens
a "Context Usage" card above the composer: how full the window is, a
segmented bar and one row per category; "View Report" opens the same
breakdown as a Markdown document with its preview. The adapter side is
Claude Agent (Plus) 0.38.0's `_claude/context/usage`, advertised as
`_claude/context`.

- acp_thread: context_usage::ContextUsageReport, read from plus's answer
  (categories with an optional stable id, tools by call and result,
  MCP tools by server, memory files, skills, subagents). Unknown fields
  are ignored and a category's id is optional, as the SDK asks.
  AgentConnection gains supports_context_usage and context_usage; the
  default refuses.
- agent_servers (v1): `_claude/context/usage` {sessionId} through
  send_task_request when the agent advertises `_claude/context`.
  parse_context_usage_answer reads `ok` strictly (a missing field is
  named, never a zero) and passes `unavailable`'s reason through.
- agent_ui: the ring's click keeps its quota refresh (§6.16) and also
  opens or closes the card (ContextUsageCard, per thread view). It is
  asked for on a click only: plus's full count costs token-count calls,
  and while a turn runs plus answers an estimate, which the card says.
  The card keeps to the composer's column (content_column, §6.30), sits
  under the docked tasks bar and above a pending question, and paints
  each category by its SDK id from the theme's accents (the system
  prompt muted): the agent's colour is the CLI's theme name, which Zeo's
  themes do not have. Free space and the compaction buffer are the bar's
  empty part, not rows.
- "View Report" writes context_usage_markdown into an untitled Markdown
  buffer (open_markdown_in_workspace, as Open Thread as Markdown does)
  and dispatches markdown::OpenPreview on it: thread title, repository,
  window size, tokens used, model and auto-compact, an explanation of
  the window, a table of categories with their share, then one section
  per category saying what it is and whether it is the agent's or the
  user's to control, with its sub-rows as a table. Sub-rows sent without
  their category get a section of their own, so nothing is dropped.

Tests: v1::context_usage_tests (6) read plus's answer -- whole, unknown
fields and ids tolerated, the mid-turn estimate, a missing field named,
`unavailable`'s reason, an unknown status; context_usage_card::tests (6)
-- a category keeps its colour wherever it sorts, unknown rows never share
one, shares of the window, no overflow past the bar, a zero window, the
labels; context_usage_report::tests (3) -- the Markdown as a snapshot, a
full count without the estimate note, thousands grouped. Seen failing:
four probes at once, each on its own function (the bar's scale removed,
unknown rows painted by position alone, orphan sub-rows dropped,
`unavailable`'s reason replaced) failed exactly those four tests. Xvfb
proof with a stub agent in the hub:
docs/assets/zeo-6.34-context-card-2026-11-15/ (the stub received
`_claude/context/usage` {"sessionId": "stub-context"} once per opening;
the report opened as "Context Usage" beside its preview).
---

